# =====================================================================
# ALLOWLIST .gitignore -- denies everything by default.
#
# This working tree holds ~100 real client workbooks and data CSVs
# (named groups, premiums, loss ratios, broker/RSD performance) spread
# across ~30 directories, plus ~1 GB of built exes. A denylist would
# only have to miss ONE pattern to publish client data to GitHub, so
# this file ignores everything and re-adds source code explicitly.
#
# Consequence to know: a NEW source file in a new location is ignored
# by default too. If `git status` doesn't show a file you just wrote,
# add an allow rule below -- don't use `git add -f`, which defeats the
# point of failing safe.
# =====================================================================

# 1. Deny everything.
*

# 2. Allow descent into directories so the allowlist in step 4 can match.
!*/

# 3. Re-block heavy, data-only, and generated trees. Listing a directory
#    here stops git descending into it at all -- faster than ignoring its
#    files individually, and it cannot be re-opened by a later rule.
All-Data/
FillData/
FillData---DONE/
newData/
data/
upload*/
test/
dist_combined/
dist_bundles/
node_modules/
**/_seed_stage/
**/_seed_stage_data/
**/_state_backup*/
**/_removed_synthetic*/
**/backup_*/
**/data/uploads/
**/build/pyi/
**/build/embed/
**/__pycache__/
.venv/
venv/

# 4. Allow source code back in.
#    Python (both backends, the gateway, and the root packager)
!**/*.py
#    PyInstaller specs -- hand-written build config, not generated output
!**/build/*.spec
#    Frontend source + its config (src/ is 100% code, no data assets)
!frontend/src/**
!frontend/index.html
!frontend/vite.config.js
!frontend/package.json
!frontend/package-lock.json
#    The BUILT frontend is committed on purpose (864 KB, 6 files). Azure App
#    Service detects one language per app: for a Python app it installs
#    requirements.txt but will never run `npm`, and this folder IS the UI the
#    renewal backend serves at "/". Committing it means deployment needs no CI
#    build step and no Node on the server. Rebuild with `npm run build` in
#    frontend/ and commit the result whenever the UI changes.
!frontend/dist/**
#    Infrastructure-as-code and deployment scripts (infra/)
!**/*.bicep
!**/*.ps1
!**/*.bicepparam
#    Container build
!Dockerfile
#    Dependency manifests and docs
!**/requirements.txt
!**/*.md
!.gitignore
!.dockerignore

# 5. Backstop: hard-deny every data/binary format, last word over step 4.
#    Nothing in the allowlist above legitimately uses these extensions,
#    so this can only ever catch a mistake.
*.xlsx
*.xlsm
*.xls
*.xlsb
*.csv
*.joblib
*.pkl
*.pickle
*.parquet
*.db
*.sqlite*
*.exe
*.zip
*.7z
*.log
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.ico
*.pdf
*.txt.bak
*.bak
*.bak_*
.env
.env.*

# 6. Re-allowed after the step-5 backstop, which would otherwise catch these by
#    extension. Branding assets (source) and the built frontend (the deployed
#    UI -- see step 4). Listed last because in .gitignore the last matching
#    rule wins.
!frontend/public/favicon.ico
!frontend/public/favicon.png
!frontend/public/logo.png
!frontend/dist/**
